  "reasoning": "The fact describes that the defendant used violence and threats to impede traffic police officers from performing their duties lawfully. Under Chinese criminal law, this conduct constitutes the crime of obstructing public officials in the performance of their duties, which is codified as the crime of 妨害公务 (obstructing official duties). No other criminal conduct is mentioned, so the appropriate charge is 妨害公务.",
